{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The binary-size budget","anchor":"The-binary-size-budget"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"code":"swift build -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"code":"ScreenStates","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each store their running ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a private ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, read by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every one of those ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s captures ","type":"text"},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a ","type":"text"},{"code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"code":"load(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A parent view that reads ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"text":" (via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"code":"store.isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the pattern ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property read in a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This guarantee is about ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" case could be affected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Performance","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ConcurrencyAndCancellation":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The guarantees "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes about overlapping, cancelled, and reset calls."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","title":"Concurrency & Cancellation","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/concurrencyandcancellation"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/isRefreshing":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isRefreshing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","role":"symbol","title":"isRefreshing","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","te